Also renamed `sort_field` to `sort_order` in the client query, because this is eventually going to include enums, not just fields. Open to other naming ideas (`sort_by`?) but "field" didn't seem right.


Example query
```
{
  organizations(sortOrder: NAME, sortOrder: DESC) {
    id
    organizationName
  }
  projects(sortOrder: ORGANIZATION_AND_NAME, sortOrder: ASC) {
    projectName
    organization {
      organizationName
    }
  }
}

```

Implement `proc` definition, parsing, and evaluation:

```
proc {
  return 42;
}
```

Currently the only statement is a terminal `return`.
